// XFAIL: RT-468: WRONG CODE at -O2: the discriminant of a `#[repr(i64)]` enum is computed in i32: `A = 2000000000 * 2` is refused at -O0 ("this constant expression overflows") and is -294967296 at -O2; rustc types it with the repr, i64, and prints 4000000000 (0.30.2)
// From the re-review of the integer-literal work (t302int). Since v0.30.1 at least.
// The shift form is rt_468b.
// EXPECT: 4000000000
#[repr(i64)]
enum E { A = 2000000000 * 2 }

fn main() {
    println("{}", E::A as i64);
}
